From c9de36dfb70192f738d9a779c4ded01dd4121901 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:29:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge, settings: dovi_tool's default CM v4.0 part as
 an expert switch

<video><dvcm40default>true</dvcm40default></video> in advancedsettings.xml
sends a frame whose RPU has no content mapping v4.0 part with the one that
dovi_tool adds as its "safe" default (add_cmv4_default_metadata,
CmV40DmData::default_safe()): level 3 with no offsets, level 9 DCI-P3 D65,
level 11 cinema with a D65 white point, level 254 of CM v4.0.2, and no
level 8 or 10. The blocks are converted for the tunnel as an RPU's are
(dvbridge_cm4_wire()), after the v2.9 part.

It is a test of what a display of display management 4 does with such a
stream, to be judged on the display: no conversion of the v2.9 trims
(level 8 has no public definition to convert them to), and dovi_tool
itself calls it unsafe. Off by default; never for a display of display
management 2 or 3 or where the v4.0 part is left out; a frame whose payload
has no room for it goes out without it. kodi.log says when it is on and,
once in a stream, when it is added.
